    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and it passes. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `title` \u2192 `salutation` feature for `POST /api/owners` (input) and `GET /api/owners/{id}` (output), keeping each piece of logic in its proper layer:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `title` as an optional write field on `OwnerFields` (enum `MR`/`MRS`/`MS`/`DR`) and `salutation` as a derived `readOnly` field on `Owner`. Both DTOs are generated from this spec.\n\n2. **`Owner` entity** \u2014 added the persisted `title` column/field with getter/setter, so the value survives from create to the later GET.\n\n3. **DB schemas** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `title` column so the entity maps cleanly across all supported databases.\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 added a `salutation(owner)` derivation (`title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title), wired via `@Mapping(target = \"salutation\", ...)`, alongside the existing derived fields. The `title` input field maps automatically through the existing `toOwner`/`toOwnerDto` mappings (MapStruct handles the enum\u2194String conversion).\n\nNo pipeline function classes needed changing \u2014 `BuildOwner` maps the whole `OwnerFieldsDto` (now including `title`) via the mapper, and the responder derives `salutation` at serialization time.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreComposesSalutation` (and the full suite) passes: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
